              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible risk of undefined behavior due to overlapping memory regions between the source and destination buffers in the memory copy operation. The destination and source expressions are both identifiers, and dataflow analysis suggests that the destination buffer may alias or overlap with the source buffer. Additionally, there is no explicit check or guard in the code to prevent this overlap, and the source pointer may also be null at this call site, which could lead to further undefined behavior. The use of a pointer type for the destination without a known capacity further increases the risk. These factors together indicate a real risk of undefined behavior, which can lead to security vulnerabilities or program crashes.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap. If there is any possibility of overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`, as `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. Before performing the copy, you can also add explicit checks to ensure the buffers do not overlap:\n\n```cpp\n// Example check for overlap (assuming pointers and known sizes)\nif ((buf + sizeof(pltData) <= pltData) || (pltData + sizeof(pltData) <= buf)) {\n    memcpy(buf, pltData, sizeof(pltData));\n} else {\n    // Use memmove if overlap is possible\n    memmove(buf, pltData, sizeof(pltData));\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you know that overlap is not possible by design, document this assumption clearly in the code and add assertions to enforce it:\n\n```cpp\nassert((buf + sizeof(pltData) <= pltData) || (pltData + sizeof(pltData) <= buf));\nmemcpy(buf, pltData, sizeof(pltData));\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n___\n"
