            {
              "id": "94f46ffa-57eb-3f1f-9d38-2f223c5be768",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the destination buffer's capacity is not known at the point of the memory copy operation, and there is no evidence that the number of bytes being copied (4) is guaranteed to fit into the destination buffer. The source is a string literal, which means there is no risk of overlapping memory regions or null pointer dereference. However, the lack of information about the size of the destination buffer (which is a pointer type) means that a buffer overflow could occur if the buffer is not large enough. This is a common source of security vulnerabilities in C/C++ code, especially when dealing with raw pointers and memory operations.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore performing the memory copy, ensure that the destination buffer is at least 4 bytes in size. If the buffer is dynamically allocated, check its size before copying. For example:\n\n```cpp\n// Ensure 'buf' points to a buffer of at least 4 bytes before this call\nif (buf != nullptr /* && buffer_size >= 4 */) {\n    memcpy(buf, \"\\177ELF\", 4);\n}\n```\nIf the buffer is allocated elsewhere, document and assert its size:\n\n```cpp\nassert(buf != nullptr);\n// If possible, also assert the buffer's size\n// assert(buffer_size >= 4);\nmemcpy(buf, \"\\177ELF\", 4);\n```\nIf you control the allocation, allocate the buffer with at least 4 bytes:\n\n```cpp\nuint8_t buf[4];\nmemcpy(buf, \"\\177ELF\", 4);\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
